    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204702": {
      "title": "Operations and Event Assistant (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Operations and Event Assistant (Part-Time) Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Operations and Event Assistant (Part-Time) Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Operations and Event Assistant (Part-Time) Category: Education Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Engagement Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 204702 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: BASIC FUNCTION: The Office of Student Engagement (OSE) promotes student success and engagement by focusing on three areas: co-curricular learning, leadership, and student development. The Operations and Event Assistant will help manage the day-to-day facility and event operations of Gerety Hall and the Papitto Pavilion. This includes overseeing the welcome desk customer service experience in the evening hours, providing support to the Gerety Hall Student Workers, managing facility amenities, and ensuring the successful execution of programs within these specific venues. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Gerety Hall and Papitto Pavilion Operations: Provide coverage and support at the Gerety Hall Welcome Desk during evening hours, serving as a welcoming resource and primary point of contact for students, staff, and guests. Assist in the daily operations of the Gerety Hall Student Center and the Papitto Pavilion, helping to ensure spaces remain welcoming, clean, and orderly. Support Gerety Hall Student Workers in preparing spaces for events, checking in hosts, and completing post-event breakdown and resetting as needed. Support the operations of specialized building amenities, including the golf simulator, by helping to monitor proper usage and equipment condition. Serve as an on-site point of contact for facility incidents during shifts. Assist in capturing and maintaining records and program data to support office-wide assessment efforts. Participate in university-wide yield programs and events, including open houses,     Connection Day, and other traditional programs Work major events for the Office of Student Engagement, such as Fall Festival Weekend, Spring Week, Orientation, and Senior Week. Evening or weekend hours will be required. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Performs other duties as may be assigned by the Director of Student Engagement. This position is classified as an \"essential position\". During the academic year, when students are on-campus, employees who occupy an essential position (\"essential personnel\"), may be required to be on campus during emergencies, when work and/or classes have been cancelled. Essential personnel will be notified by their supervisor if they're required to be on-campus during such emergencies. LICENSES, TOOLS, AND EQUIPMENT: Valid driver's license required. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS: The incumbent is not subject to adverse environmental conditions. WORK SCHEDULE: Part-time, 25-hours per week, 10-months per year Requirements: Required : High school diploma or GED Valid driver's license required. One (1) year of administrative, customer service, office support, hospitality, or event-related experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated customer service skills with the ability to interact professionally with diverse populations. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Ability to lift and move materials weighing up to 25 pounds and assist with event setup and breakdown. Willingness to work evenings and weekends in support of events. Preferred : Associate's degree in business administration, communications, hospitality, event management, or a related field. Experience coordinating meetings, conferences, or special events. Experience working in a higher education, nonprofit, or customer-facing office environment. Familiarity with event registration or scheduling software Experience providing front desk reception and executive administrative support. Additional Information: Salve Regina University strives to provide equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, marital or parental status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal or state law, in the administration of Salve Regina's employment policies, education policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other University administered programs. In accordance with Title IX, it does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any of its educational programs or activities. Salve Regina is also committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    },
    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204580": {
      "title": "Club Sport Coach, Men's Volleyball (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Club Sport Coach, Men's Volleyball (Part-Time) Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Club Sport Coach, Men's Volleyball (Part-Time) Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Club Sport Coach, Men's Volleyball (Part-Time) Category: Education Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Dean of Students Office Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 8, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 204580 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: BASIC FUNCTION Develop and supervise the Club Men's Volleyball team in accordance with institutional and departmental objectives within the rules and regulations of the governing bodies for Salve Regina University Rec Sports. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Instruct student-athletes in the rules, fundamentals, and team concepts of volleyball.  Provide team supervision at practices and competitions both on and off campus. Develop and implement practices and competitions to provide a positive and competitive experience for players. Establish team rules and protocols and implement and enforce appropriately. Maintain a roster that is as inclusive as possible without sacrificing the quality of the program or safety of the team members. Build a network of college club programs and athletic contests that are an appropriate match for our team to compete against. Inventory and monitor equipment and facility to ensure it is safe and maintained in its proper state. Meet regularly with the Director of Recreation to evaluate roster, budget and schedule. Monitor your Salve Regina University email account and respond to inquiries from prospective students in a timely manner.  On occasion, represent the university and team at recruitment related events. Adhere to the policies and guidelines set forth by the University and the Dean of Students department. Abide by and enforce the rules and regulations of the Club Sport Conference and Competition agencies and venues. Club sport coaches shall immediately advise the Director of Recreation if there is a reason to believe that violations have occurred or will occur in regard to sexual misconduct or harassment, hazing, or any other action or activity that could endanger the well being of a team member. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with the team's annual campus wide event relating to their sport. Requirements: Required Qualifications A passion for the university's work in creating a diverse and inclusive community is expected. Must be a self-starter and problem solver. Must have the ability to work independently. Experience in mentoring high school and/or college students. Strong interpersonal communication skills and ability to provide constructive feedback. High School diploma or equivalent. Valid Driver's license. Preferred Qualifications Baccalaureate degree. Competitive athletic experience. Coaching experience at the high school, club or college level. Chauffer's license or willingness and ability to obtain equivalent endorsement. Additional Information: Salve Regina University strives to provide equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, marital or parental status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal or state law, in the administration of Salve Regina's employment policies, education policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other University administered programs. In accordance with Title IX, it does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any of its educational programs or activities. Salve Regina is also committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    },
    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204870": {
      "title": "MFA Program Director (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: MFA Program Director (Part-Time) Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: MFA Program Director (Part-Time) Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details MFA Program Director (Part-Time) Category: Education Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Graduate and Professional Studies Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 204870 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: BASIC FUNCTION: The Program Coordinator provides academic and administrative leadership for the Master of Fine Arts (MFA) program. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Plan and oversee the Winter and Summer residencies in collaboration with the Program Founder and Co-Director. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Serve as the primary liaison between the Graduate Program faculty and University administration on matters related to the program. Develop and maintain program planning documents, including strategic goals, annual reports, academic program reviews, self-studies, assessment plans, and accreditation reports for submission to the Vice Provost. Develop, manage, and administer the program's annual operating budget, including identifying capital needs and ensuring expenditures remain within approved budget allocations. Review curriculum planning and course scheduling in collaboration with faculty, the Department Chair, the Registrar, and the Vice Provost. Ensure that current course syllabi are submitted each semester to the Office of Graduate and Professional Studies. Recruit, recommend, and evaluate adjunct faculty in collaboration with the Department Chair and Vice Provost, consistent with University policies. Oversee the graduate admissions process by reviewing applications and making admission decisions in accordance with established program and University policies. Monitor student recruitment, retention, academic progress, and graduation to ensure compliance with University, departmental, and program requirements. Coordinate academic advising or directly advise students regarding curriculum planning, degree progression, University policies, and professional or career opportunities. Collaborate with Admissions and Marketing & Communications to promote the program, support recruitment initiatives, and increase enrollment. WORK SCHEDULE: This is a part-time, 15-hour per week, 9-month per year position (October 1 - June 30) LICENSES, TOOLS, AND EQUIPMENT: N/A ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS: N/A Requirements: Required : An MFA or equivalent doctoral/terminal degree in Creative Writing, Theatre, Visual arts, or Film. At least three years previous leadership in academic settings; Experience planning and coordinating events. Preferred : Active national or international standing as an artist, writer, or practitioner. Additional Information: Salve Regina University strives to provide equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, marital or parental status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal or state law, in the administration of Salve Regina's employment policies, education policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other University administered programs. In accordance with Title IX, it does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any of its educational programs or activities. Salve Regina is also committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    },
    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205097": {
      "title": "Box Office Manager (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Box Office Manager (Part-Time) Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Box Office Manager (Part-Time) Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Box Office Manager (Part-Time) Category: Education Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Theatre Arts Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 205097 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: BASIC FUNCTION: Oversee Box Office/Ticket sales for all Music, Theatre and Dance events and productions at the Casino Theatre, Megley Blackbox, and Ochre Court. Ensure Box Office issues are resolved around the clock. Manage the house during performances. Assist with coordination of production-related elements. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: The specific duties and responsibilities for this position include but are not limited to: Act as house manager for all events as needed; train and schedule all other house managers, box office staff, ushers and volunteers. Maintain the Music, Theatre and Dance season calendar; schedule rehearsals and performances so they appear on the University calendar. Market Music, Theatre and Dance events to audiences beyond Salve through local events calendars and Mailchimp e-blasts. Communicate with university offices including Marketing & Communications, Safety & Security, and University Events and Conference Services as needed. Schedule equipment load-ins and loadouts, piano moves and tunings, ushers, parking, security, concessions, and custodial coverage for rehearsals and events. Communicate building, event, and life safety policies and procedures. Complete additional duties and/or responsibilities as assigned. WORK SCHEDULE: Approximately up to 20 hours/week during the academic year not including holidays or winter break.  October - May. Requirements: Required : Associate's degree in theatre or dance. House management experience. Ability and willingness to regularly work a flexible and varied schedule including evenings and weekends. Strong leadership and interpersonal skills. Proven ability to problem solve and work with people. Ability to maintain organization, strict accuracy and be detail-oriented. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work independently as well as with others and be self-motivated. Preferred : Bachelor's degree in theatre or dance preferred. Additional Information: Salve Regina University strives to provide equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, marital or parental status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal or state law, in the administration of Salve Regina's employment policies, education policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other University administered programs. In accordance with Title IX, it does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any of its educational programs or activities. Salve Regina is also committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    },
    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205096": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Groundskeeper Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Groundskeeper Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Groundskeeper Category: Education Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities/Grounds Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205096 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: BASIC FUNCTION: Work in all areas of the Grounds Department according to capabilities, and needs of the University. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Primary duties involve performing various skilled and non-skilled tasks in the general, preventive, emergency, and predictive maintenance of grounds and interior planting as well as equipment and machinery associated with these operations.  Perform setup and distribution tasks, as required. Work will include (but is not limited to): lawn care (seeding, springing and sodding, mowing, fertilizing, spreading lime, mulching, thatching, weed control, watering, trimming, edging) yard waste maintenance of trees and shrubs (protection from equipment, people and weather, watering, trimming, fertilizing, cultivation, mulching, pruning, grading, repairs, planting, replacing) flowers (planting, removal, water filtration, development of beds, weeding) leaf removal, brush removal, walkways and parking areas (repairs, sweeping, weeding, sealing, markers) permanent and temporary fences, retaining walls, exterior stairs, curbs, traffic islands, site drainage, playgrounds, site furnishings, bike racks, water control, site irrigation snow removal, de-icing, tracks, courts, athletic playing surfaces, such as but not limited to soccer, football and baseball facilities, bleachers site lighting, flagpoles, courtyards, interior plants and planting areas soil management in regards to proper fertilization and maintaining appropriate ground cover, trash and litter control, graphics, bird and pest control and other work associated with landscaping and groundskeeping operations. Remove trash and recycling across campus. This position is classified as an \"essential position\". Employees who occupy an essential position (\"essential personnel\"), may be required to be on campus during emergencies, when work and/or classes have been cancelled. Exceptions may apply and will be determined by the department/office supervisor on a case-by-case basis. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Work with other Grounds department team members in a professional, supportive and courteous manner in carrying out responsibilities of this position. Work and prepare work using acceptable/standard methods tools, equipment and practices related to facilities and grounds activities. May be required to perform duties such as custodial or maintenance during emergency, or critical situations as may be directed by the AVP of Facilities Management. LICENSES, TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT: Valid driver's license required. Must have a home telephone service that allows Management or Security the ability to contact you. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS: This position is subject to outside work and extreme cold and hot temperatures may be encountered in this position.  The potential exists where noise, vibration, hazards and atmospheric conditions might also be encountered.  Use of protective equipment is required.  The employee must be especially aware of any impact on safety and security. Requirements: Required : High school diploma or GED required. Minimum of one year grounds experience or equivalent combination of education and experience. Working knowledge of groundskeeping operations and equipment. Ability to work overtime, when required. Ability to establish and maintain good working relationships with supervisor, fellow coworkers and students. Must be neat in appearance. Must be able to lift and carry 80 pounds. Preferred : 1+ years of grounds experience. Additional Information: Salve Regina University offers generous benefits to eligible employees including (waiting periods apply): health, dental and vision coverage available on the first of the month following date of hire 403(b) retirement plan through TIAA with employee and employer contributions as well as access to advising services long-term disability coverage employer-paid life and AD&D insurance up to 100% free tuition at Salve for eligible employees and qualified dependents robust wellness program and free access to the on-campus Fitness Center Other available benefits include: supplemental life insurance for employees and dependents supplemental insurance coverage through Aflac Tuition Exchange scholarship program. Application available for qualified dependents of eligible employees working full-time discounted pet insurance through ASPCA student loan forgiveness assistance program (SAVI) employee Assistance Program through Health Advocate flexible spending health and dependent care accounts health savings accounts 529 collegebound saver program paid parental leave and adoption assistance For more detailed information on Salve's benefits, visit https://salve.edu/human-resources/benefits . Salve Regina University strives to cultivate belonging values through diversity, equity inclusion in order to foster a welcoming culture for our staff, faculty and students, as well as the wider community.  Salve Regina University embraces all people with grace. No matter the path traveled to get here, the University acknowledges that many identities will intersect. Salve Regina belongs to all in its community. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    },
    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205094": {
      "title": "Event Specialist",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Event Specialist Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Event Specialist Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Event Specialist Category: Education Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: University Events & Conference Services Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205094 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: BASIC FUNCTION: The Event Specialist provides consistent on-site execution and operational support for University Events & Conference Services (UECS) events, conferences, weddings, summer programs, and selected internal University events. The position is designed primarily to provide evening and weekend coverage, serving as an on-site University representative and ensuring that events are executed safely, professionally, and in accordance with confirmed plans and University policies. By assuming a significant share of event-day execution, the Event Specialist creates capacity for UECS professional staff to focus on client relationships, planning, sales, revenue development, and long-term account stewardship. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Event & Conference Execution Oversee on-site execution of assigned weddings, external events, conferences, camps, and selected internal University events, including event timelines, guest arrival, program flow, and breakdown. Serve as the primary on-site UECS contact during assigned events; communicate with clients, conference organizers, vendors, campus partners, and guests and escalate issues when appropriate. Confirm assigned facilities are guest-ready prior to event start and that setup, service, and breakdown align with approved plans, diagrams, BEOs, contracts, and University policies. Coordinate vendor arrival, access, setup, service, and departure, including caterers, rental companies, florists, entertainment, photographers, transportation providers, and other event partners. Troubleshoot last-minute operational issues and coordinate with Public Safety, Facilities/Grounds, Housekeeping, Dining Services, Media/IT Services, and other University departments as needed. Provide tours, photo-session coverage, and other client-facing event support as assigned. Conference, GRC & Summer Program Support Provide evening and weekend staffing for conferences and camps, including arrival, check-in, meeting, program, and departure support. Support Gordon Research Conferences (GRC), including conference check-in coverage as scheduled and provide increased UECS supervision and operational presence for GRC poster sessions and coordinate issues with appropriate campus partners. Support summer conference operations and Salve Institute summer programming as assigned, including guest-facing logistics, space readiness, resource coordination, and evening/weekend coverage. Provide UECS presence at selected internal University events when departmental operational support is requested. Communication, Compliance & Documentation Review event information, timelines, diagrams, BEOs, and operational notes prior to assigned events and communicate relevant updates to the Wedding Events Manager and other UECS staff. Monitor compliance with University event policies, vendor requirements, facility-use standards, and risk-management expectations. Document significant event issues, damages, vendor concerns, client feedback, and follow-up items for UECS staff. Help protect University facilities by monitoring event activity and providing additional on-site oversight, particularly in high-use historic spaces such as Ochre Court. Teamwork and other responsibilities Report to and work closely with the Wedding Events Manager; collaborate with the Conference & University Scheduling Manager, Director, Executive Director, and other UECS staff. Assist with training and direction of student event staff or temporary support personnel assigned to events. Support departmental projects, tours, showcases, and other revenue-generating or revenue-enabling activities as assigned. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Perform other job-related duties as assigned. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS: This position is subject to both inside and outside work, where extreme cold and hot temperatures can be encountered. Requirements: Required : High school diploma/GED and a minimum of 2 years of event, hospitality, conference, venue, customer-service, or related operational experience; equivalent combinations of education and experience may be considered. Demonstrated ability to manage event timelines, coordinate multiple parties, and respond calmly and effectively to unexpected situations. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills and a strong customer-service orientation. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, sound judgment, and ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment. Ability and willingness to work a schedule concentrated on evenings and weekends, primarily Friday-Tuesday, with flexibility based on the University event calendar. Ability to travel throughout campus and work indoors and outdoors in varying weather conditions. Preferred : Experience with weddings, conferences, higher education, hospitality/banquet operations, or historic venues. Experience coordinating vendors and working with event diagrams, BEOs, timelines, or event-management systems. Additional Information: Salve Regina University offers generous benefits to eligible employees including (waiting periods apply): health, dental and vision coverage available on the first of the month following date of hire 403(b) retirement plan through TIAA with employee and employer contributions as well as access to advising services long-term disability coverage employer-paid life and AD&D insurance up to 100% free tuition at Salve for eligible employees and qualified dependents robust wellness program and free access to the on-campus Fitness Center Other available benefits include: supplemental life insurance for employees and dependents supplemental insurance coverage through Aflac Tuition Exchange scholarship program. Application available for qualified dependents of eligible employees working full-time discounted pet insurance through ASPCA student loan forgiveness assistance program (SAVI) employee Assistance Program through Health Advocate flexible spending health and dependent care accounts health savings accounts 529 collegebound saver program paid parental leave and adoption assistance For more detailed information on Salve's benefits, visit https://salve.edu/human-resources/benefits . Salve Regina University strives to cultivate belonging values through diversity, equity inclusion in order to foster a welcoming culture for our staff, faculty and students, as well as the wider community.  Salve Regina University embraces all people with grace. No matter the path traveled to get here, the University acknowledges that many identities will intersect. Salve Regina belongs to all in its community. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    },
    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204966": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper (Temporary)",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Groundskeeper (Temporary) Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Groundskeeper (Temporary) Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Groundskeeper (Temporary) Category: Education Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities/Grounds Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 18, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Temporary Position ID: 204966 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: BASIC FUNCTION: Work in all areas of the Grounds Department according to capabilities, and needs of the University. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Primary duties involve performing various skilled and non-skilled tasks in the general, preventive, emergency, and predictive maintenance of grounds and interior planting as well as equipment and machinery associated with these operations.  Perform setup and distribution tasks, as required. Work will include (but is not limited to): lawn care (seeding, springing and sodding, mowing, fertilizing, spreading lime, mulching, thatching, weed control, watering, trimming, edging) yard waste maintenance of trees and shrubs (protection from equipment, people and weather, watering, trimming, fertilizing, cultivation, mulching, pruning, grading, repairs, planting, replacing) flowers (planting, removal, water filtration, development of beds, weeding) leaf removal, brush removal, walkways and parking areas (repairs, sweeping, weeding, sealing, markers) permanent and temporary fences, retaining walls, exterior stairs, curbs, traffic islands, site drainage, playgrounds, site furnishings, bike racks, water control, site irrigation snow removal, de-icing, tracks, courts, athletic playing surfaces, such as but not limited to soccer, football and baseball facilities, bleachers site lighting, flagpoles, courtyards, interior plants and planting areas soil management in regards to proper fertilization and maintaining appropriate ground cover, trash and litter control, graphics, bird and pest control and other work associated with landscaping and groundskeeping operations. Remove trash and recycling across campus. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Work with other Grounds department team members in a professional, supportive and courteous manner in carrying out responsibilities of this position. Work and prepare work using acceptable/standard methods tools, equipment and practices related to facilities and grounds activities. May be required to perform duties such as custodial or maintenance during emergency, or critical situations as may be directed by the AVP of Facilities Management. This position is classified as an \"essential position\". Employees who occupy an essential position (\"essential personnel\"), may be required to be on campus during emergencies, when work and/or classes have been cancelled. Exceptions may apply and will be determined by the department/office supervisor on a case-by-case basis. WORK SCHEDULE: This is a full-time, 35-hours per week, temporary position with a tentative end date scheduled for the end of November 2026. LICENSES, TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT: Valid driver's license required. Must have a home telephone service that allows Management or Security the ability to contact you. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS: This position is subject to outside work and extreme cold and hot temperatures may be encountered in this position.  The potential exists where noise, vibration, hazards and atmospheric conditions might also be encountered.  Use of protective equipment is required.  The employee must be especially aware of any impact on safety and security. Requirements: Required: High school diploma or GED required. Minimum of one year grounds experience or equivalent combination of education and experience. Working knowledge of groundskeeping operations and equipment. Ability to work overtime, when required. Ability to establish and maintain good working relationships with supervisor, fellow coworkers and students. Must be neat in appearance. Must be able to lift and carry 80 pounds. Preferred: 1+ years of grounds experience. Additional Information: Salve Regina University strives to provide equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, marital or parental status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal or state law, in the administration of Salve Regina's employment policies, education policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other University administered programs. In accordance with Title IX, it does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any of its educational programs or activities. Salve Regina is also committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    }
